# Repo files Prettier must not reformat on save in VS Code. The repo's style is in
# .prettierrc.json (tabs, like .editorconfig); without it, the repo would inherit the global
# ~/.prettierrc.json.

# Nested lists use 4 spaces (.claude/rules/documentation.md) and Prettier realigns them to 2.
# tools/check-docs.ps1 watches their structure.
*.md

# Copies of dotfiles-parrot's files (the prompt theme and the global style): reformatting them
# here would make them drift apart.
10-shell/oh-my-posh/capr4n.omp.json
40-format/

# This repo is the Claude Code layer's source (Parrot will take it from here). Its files mix
# styles; unifying them is a change of its own, not something format on save should do.
50-claude/

# `winget export` format (curated by hand): winget's format is kept so that copying entries from
# an export produces no format diffs.
60-apps/*.json
# Windows Terminal rewrites its whole settings.json (4 spaces) every time a setting changes from
# its UI: reformatting it would give a huge diff on each change.
20-terminal/windows-terminal/settings.json
